WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.063
The separation gate puts the leaver
in the Federal Modernization

2
00:00:04.063 --> 00:00:07.200
Workbook's Book 03's order
and then proves the timing.

3
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.338
Disable the account and
revoke its sessions first.

4
00:00:10.338 --> 00:00:13.768
Then one custom task starts
the device retire and the

5
00:00:13.768 --> 00:00:17.276
card revocation together,
and waits for both to report.

6
00:00:17.276 --> 00:00:21.955
That wait can run from thirty minutes
to three hours, and if it times out,

7
00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:25.425
it goes to a high-priority
exception, not a retry loop.

8
00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:29.300
Then come the removals, and a
read-back to confirm the block took.

9
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.612
A disabled account with live
sessions is an incident.

10
00:00:32.612 --> 00:00:37.625
Deletion comes last, in a separate
workflow, after the devices are retired.

11
00:00:37.625 --> 00:00:39.445
Set the leave time late in the day,

12
00:00:39.445 --> 00:00:42.412
and remember the schedule is
part of the time allowed.

13
00:00:42.412 --> 00:00:45.613
An emergency means an
immediate out-of-band block,

14
00:00:45.613 --> 00:00:48.813
then the same sequence on
demand, behind approval.

15
00:00:48.813 --> 00:00:51.392
A separation entered more than three days

16
00:00:51.392 --> 00:00:53.825
late misses the trigger,
so run it by hand.

17
00:00:53.825 --> 00:00:56.180
Privileged leavers need their own path.
